# Forge system — upstream provenance
#
# This directory vendors the AI-SDLC agent operating system from:
#
#   repo:    https://github.com/mock-server/mockserver-monorepo
#   commit:  7febd65f0815caf57855fae54ba3df3915376cc6
#   date:    2026-07-06
#   license: Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE-upstream in this directory)
#   author:  James Bloom / MockServer project
#
# Layout:
#   engine/    Tier-1 files, kept byte-identical to upstream wherever possible so
#              `diff -r` against a fresh clone shows (a) our deliberate changes and
#              (b) upstream improvements to pull. Deliberate modifications carry a
#              one-line "# forge: modified from upstream — <reason>" marker.
#   template/  Tier-2 files derived from upstream with project-specific regions
#              replaced by {{FORGE_*}} tokens and <!-- FORGE:REGION ... --> blocks.
#              These are NOT byte-identical; diff against upstream at the section level.
#   seeds/     Tier-3 material generated fresh per install (eval task templates,
#              per-stack validation snippets). No upstream counterpart.
#
# Known deliberate deviations from upstream @ 7febd65f:
#   - engine/.opencode/scripts/{acquire,release}-commit-lock.sh: generic error message
#     (was "the MockServer repository").
#   - BUG FIXES found during e2e testing (candidates to report upstream):
#     1. engine/.opencode/scripts/agent-status.sh: resolves the MAIN checkout via
#        `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` — upstream's --show-toplevel returns the
#        worktree root when run from inside a worktree (the default place sessions
#        live), so it never found .worktrees/.
#     2. template/.opencode/rules/worktree-workflow.md + .claude/commands/worktree-merge.md:
#        rebase lock path uses the shared git common dir — upstream's relative
#        ".git/agent-rebase.lock" breaks inside a worktree, where .git is a pointer
#        FILE, exactly where the merge step runs.
#     3. Same files: corrected upstream's claim that flock is "present by default on
#        macOS" (it is not; util-linux tool) — availability must be checked and the
#        mkdir mutex used as the standard fallback, never skipping the lock.
#   - rules/subagent-routing.md moved engine -> template: its conversational routing
#     table is per-project (upstream rows referenced dropped Buildkite/AWS skills);
#     now a FORGE:REGION.
#   - review-constitution.md: re-added GENERICIZED rows for 7 upstream project-specific
#     principles whose stable IDs are cited by the installed review skills (AMB-08,
#     CON-07, CON-08, SEC-11, OPS-09, OPS-10, COR-08) — deleting them left dangling
#     citations. Two truly project-specific citations fixed at the call site instead:
#     review-code SKILL CPX-11 -> CPX-01/CPX-04; review-code commands' example
#     [COR-10] -> [COR-05].
#   - Dropped as MockServer-specific ops tooling (not part of the portable system):
#     rules/aws-ids-file.md; commands/skills for aws-investigation,
#     pipeline-investigation, browser-auth, build-monitor, dependabot-snyk-pr-management,
#     docker-build-push, dockerhub-credentials, pr-monitor, prepare-release,
#     release-management, renew-test-certs, terraform-tfvars, ui-screenshots;
#     plugins/buildkite-status.ts; the changelog-specific gate content.
#   - Model routing per forge/docs/06-discussion-outcome.md: opencode → GLM 5.2 (strong)
#     / M3 (weak); Claude Code → fable (strong) / opus (weak), upstream effort values
#     kept; Codex keeps upstream's OpenAI tiers.
#   - template/.codex/ is FORGE-ORIGINAL (no upstream counterpart): upstream targets
#     opencode + Claude Code only. It makes Codex a first-class third harness:
#     config.toml + agents/*.toml (generated from .claude/agents/*.md, bodies verbatim;
#     model_reasoning_effort mirrors Claude effort since Codex agent TOML has no
#     temperature; reviewers enforced read-only via sandbox_mode), rules/forge.rules
#     (execpolicy port of the harness deny-lists), hooks.json (Stop-hook telemetry),
#     prompts/{commit,worktree-merge}.md (copies of .claude/commands/*). When syncing
#     upstream agent/command changes, re-derive the .codex copies to match.
#   - Default-branch substitution: all files keep upstream's literal `master`; the
#     installer rewrites branch references when the target repo's default branch differs
#     (recorded in the install manifest).
#
# Sync procedure: clone upstream, `diff -r engine/ <clone>` (path-mapped), review hunks,
# pull what applies, bump the commit hash + date above.
